-`src/i18n/messages.js`. The server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
+`src/i18n/messages.js`; every error code has a message in both.
+
+The language comes from the request's `Accept-Language` header: the
+supported language with the highest q-value wins. Region tags count as their
+language (`ko-KR` is `ko`), `*` stands for any language the header does not
+name, and `q=0` rules a language out. With equal q-values the language named
+first wins. When the header is missing or accepts no supported language, the
+server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (`en` or `ko`, default `en`).
